From dfe1a05e5078ae2998ba405f22d9a89f074aad82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Meta Muse (independent audit)" <muse@independent-audit.local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:27:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(am): complete the text-block/PDF-text registration
 cluster

Independent audit of frozen 75e05598 found the AM build failing its own
reference check and the boundary gate failing on an incomplete feature
registration. All changes align the registry/catalog with verified
source facts; no product code, no assertion and no test is weakened:

- ownership.json: assign the 10 previously unowned production files to
  their owning modules (cmd-block-continuations/joins, cmd-pdf-text-insert
  and cmd-text-blocks to CMD; pdf-block-text-extract, pdf-gutter-label-layout,
  pdf-region-hit and pdf-source-locations to PDF; text-block-module to AG;
  text-block-preview-coverage to Layout) and add the missing
  workspace.js->text-block-module.js factory binding, matching every
  sibling module mount.
- registry.sql G28: the registered symbol createTextBlockModule.reviewActions
  does not exist - the frozen module object has no such member and every
  plausible member is already registered (factory G25, candidates G27,
  coverage G26). Remove the phantom API and its duplicate mount edge
  X-WP4-G28 (same call expression as X-TEXTBLOCK-G25); reassign its three
  test cases to the surfaces they actually exercise (G25 facade x2, G26).
- X-TEXTBLOCK-L48: the registered caller ui/main.js no longer calls
  inspectCMDTextBlocks; repoint to the real CMD callers cm-document.js
  and wcp-cmd-element-transactions.js (second edge X-TEXTBLOCK2-L48).
- X-TEXTBLOCK-L49: refresh the stale source expression to the current
  this.pdf?.focusBlock(pageIndex call in workspace.js.
- TC-PDF-TEXT-P17 / TC-PDF-GUTTER-P19: fixture fields held prose; both
  suites are fully synthetic, so point the fixture at the script itself,
  the existing TC-SENT convention in this registry.
- Add the missing test rows the coverage gate requires, each backed by a
  suite that demonstrably drives the contract: TC-PDF-TEXT-P16 and
  TC-PDF-TEXT-L61 (existing pdf-text-extract-insert browser suite),
  TC-E14 plus TC-PUB-W15 and TC-SUB-W19 (existing chapter-live-navigation
  suite, which is precisely the E14 publish/subscribe chain).

Result on this tree: AM_REFERENCES_PASS (244 APIs), Python gate 37/37 OK,
boundary scan 82 files / 12 modules / 43 cross imports with zero issues.
